{"The align-items mixin includes `-ms-align-items: $alignment` which is not a valid CSS property and was never part of any Microsoft/IE spec - this is dead code that should be removed": 0.1770939826965332, "The `-webkit-box-ordinal-group` and `-moz-box-ordinal-group` properties in the order mixin use a 1-based ordinal group system, while the modern `order` property uses a 0-based integer - passing the same `$val` to both causes an off-by-one visual order difference in old WebKit browsers, should pass `$val + 1` to the old-spec properties": 0.7621853947639465, "The `button { float: right }` inside `.small-action` is ignored because floats have no effect on flex items after the parent was converted to a flex container - this causes the delete/remove button to lose its right-aligned position and is a visual regression": 0.8281702995300293}